<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Quantum HTML + CSS example 08_typography/16: Ellipsis for long text -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Ellipsis for long text</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #1f2933;
      background: #f5f7fa;
    }
    .demo { max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; }
    .demo > h1 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 2rem; }
    .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: #52606d; }

    .one { width: 18rem; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; background: #fff; padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; }
    .three { width: 22rem; display: -webkit-box; -webkit-box-orient: vertical; -webkit-line-clamp: 3; line-clamp: 3; overflow: hidden; background: #fff; padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="demo">
    <h1>Ellipsis for long text</h1>
    <p class="lead">Single-line truncation, and line-clamp for several lines.</p>
    <p class="one">This very long title will never fit on a single line in this box</p>
    <p class="three">Three lines at most: this paragraph keeps going well past the third line so that you can see the
    clamp in action, cutting the rest off with an ellipsis instead of growing the card taller and taller.</p>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
